cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use jwstflow in research, please cite this software and also cite
  the version of the official JWST calibration pipeline used in your
  analysis. Record the JWST pipeline version and CRDS context associated
  with the reduction where relevant.
title: jwstflow
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Lukas
    family-names: Welzel
    email: welzel@strw.leidenuniv.nl
    affiliation: Leiden Observatory, Leiden University
version: 0.1.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: https://github.com/lwelzel/jwstflow
url: https://github.com/lwelzel/jwstflow
abstract: >-
  jwstflow is a lightweight, YAML-driven orchestrator for the official
  James Webb Space Telescope calibration pipeline. It coordinates data
  acquisition, CRDS reference handling, association construction,
  pipeline and custom-step execution, checkpointing, parallel execution,
  provenance, product organization, and quality-assurance tasks to make
  JWST reductions easier to reproduce and share.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - JWST
  - data reduction
  - calibration pipeline
  - reproducible workflows
  - NIRSpec
  - MIRI
